WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.525
Why does this come first?

2
00:00:01.525 --> 00:00:03.175
Picture three writers.

3
00:00:03.175 --> 00:00:06.075
Your HR feed sets an
account's active value.

4
00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:09.475
A Lifecycle Workflows leaver
can disable the same account.

5
00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:13.625
And a help desk technician can still
edit a user's organization code.

6
00:00:13.625 --> 00:00:15.202
Each of those is a writer,

7
00:00:15.202 --> 00:00:18.987
and when two of them write the
same value, the later one wins.

8
00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:23.538
So a late active true from the pipeline
undoes the workflow's disable.

9
00:00:23.538 --> 00:00:26.398
A help desk edit to the organization code

10
00:00:26.398 --> 00:00:29.426
moves the person's access,
and HR never knows.

11
00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:32.525
In this module you fix that
before any other gate.

12
00:00:32.525 --> 00:00:37.526
You name one writer, and a backstop, for
every account-state transition and every

13
00:00:37.526 --> 00:00:42.430
HR-mastered value, and then you test the
directory audit log against that list.
